[size=5][b]Gorilla Arms let V dual-wield SMGs and shotguns.[/b][/size]

Patch 2.5 added dual-wielding through the [b]Double Trouble[/b] perk (Cool), limited to pistols and revolvers. This mod extends it: while [b]Gorilla Arms[/b] are equipped, their reinforced grip actuators steady heavier guns one-handed, so SMGs and shotguns can be paired too. Without Gorilla Arms, everything stays vanilla.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]With Gorilla Arms equipped and Double Trouble unlocked, SMGs and shotguns (including double-barrel shotguns and modded weapons of those types) can be dual-wielded.
[*]Without Gorilla Arms, only pistols and revolvers can be dual-wielded, as in vanilla. Removing Gorilla Arms unequips the off-hand SMG or shotgun.
[*]Fits the game's UI:
[list]
[*]Double Trouble's weapon box reads [i]"Only affects Power Pistols and Power Revolvers; equipping Gorilla Arms extends this to SMGs and Shotguns"[/i].
[*]Gorilla Arms get a tooltip line: [i]"Reinforced grip actuators steady SMGs and shotguns one-handed: with Double Trouble, they can be dual-wielded."[/i]
[/list]
[*]No new perk, no save data, no animation replacement. It reuses the game's own dual-wield system.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4197]TweakXL[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, or extract the archive into the Cyberpunk 2077 game folder. The files go to:
[code]r6/scripts/GorillaAkimbo/GorillaAkimbo.reds
r6/tweaks/GorillaAkimbo/GorillaAkimbo.yaml[/code]
Updating from 1.0.0 by hand: delete the old [i]r6/scripts/GorillaGrip[/i] and [i]r6/tweaks/GorillaGrip[/i] folders first.

[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
Unpair any dual-wielded SMGs or shotguns first, then remove the two files. Nothing is written to your save.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]SMGs and shotguns use the game's pistol dual-wield animations, so some reloads and hand poses look unusual.
[*]Double Trouble's own bonuses (recoil, spread, Heywood Hurricane) follow the game's rules; this mod only changes which weapons can be paired.
[*]Photo mode's weapon poses hold a single gun, so dual-wielding only shows in gameplay.
[*]Other mods that change which weapons can be dual-wielded (for example Expanded Dual Wielding or Dual Wield Anything) do the same job in a different way. Use one of them.
[/list]

[size=4][b]How it works[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]At load, a Codeware ScriptableTweak goes through all weapon and item records: it adds the game's DualWield tag to every SMG and shotgun and adds the tooltip line to Gorilla Arms.
[*]A wrap of gameItemData.CanDualWield keeps those weapon types dual-wieldable only while an item of type Cyb_StrongArms is equipped in the arms cyberware slot.
[*]A wrap of the perk tooltip adds the Gorilla Arms clause to Double Trouble's weapon box.
[*]Texts are registered through Codeware's localization system (English).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
